        <headline>yellow warning - wind - in effect</headline>
        <description>
Damaging winds are expected.

Southwesterly winds gusting to 90 km/h possible.

Where: Inland Vancouver Island.

When: Early this morning.

Remarks:
Another strong low pressure system continues to move across Vancouver Island. Strong southwesterly winds gusting to 90 km/h are possible early this morning. Winds will gradually ease later this morning as the system moves eastward.

###

Local utility outages are possible.

Please continue to monitor alerts and forecasts issued by Environment Canada. To report severe weather, send an email to BCstorm@ec.gc.ca or post reports on social media using #BCStorm.
</description>
        <instruction>
Secure loose objects. Stay away from fallen power lines.
</instruction>
